-- title:
--   Unit-root points factor through the maximal multiplicative quotient
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a henselian local domain $O$ equipped with algebra maps to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and to $\mathbb Z/p$, together with a valuation subring $P \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that the image of $O$ lies in $P$ (hypothesis `hOP`) and such that an element of $O$ dies in $\mathbb Z/p$ exactly when its image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ has $P$-valuation $<1$ (hypothesis `hres`). Let $H$ be a $p$-divisible group of height $h$ over $O$: a system of commutative rings `H.level v`, each a cocommutative $O$-Hopf algebra that is finite and free over $O$ of rank $p^{vh}$, with surjective bialgebra transition maps whose kernels are the $p^v$-torsion ideals. Let $u,\varepsilon,w$ be families of $O$-bialgebra endomorphisms of the levels with: $u$ and $\varepsilon$ and $w$ commuting with the transition maps, $\varepsilon_v\circ\varepsilon_v=\varepsilon_v$, $\varepsilon_v\circ u_v=u_v\circ\varepsilon_v$, $\varepsilon_v\circ w_v=w_v=w_v\circ\varepsilon_v$, and $w_v\circ(u_v\circ\varepsilon_v)=(u_v\circ\varepsilon_v)\circ w_v=\varepsilon_v$, so that $w$ inverts $u$ on the $\varepsilon$-part. Assume further (hypothesis `hFV`) that for every $\mathbb Z/p$-bialgebra endomorphism $F_k$ of $\mathbb Z/p\otimes_O H.\mathrm{level}\,1$ with $F_k(x)=x^p$ and every $\mathbb Z/p$-algebra endomorphism $F_D$ of its Cartier dual with $F_D(\psi)=\psi^p$, some composition power of [`CartierDual.map`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDualMap.html#L102) applied to $\mathrm{id}\otimes u_1$ equals the convolution product of $F_D\circ a$ with $b\circ \mathrm{CartierDual.map}\,F_k$ for suitable bialgebra endomorphisms $a,b$ of the dual. Fix a level $v$ and a commutative ring $Mt$ carrying a cocommutative $O$-Hopf algebra structure, finite and free over $O$, whose Cartier dual $\mathrm{CartierDual}\,O\,Mt$ is étale over $O$, together with a surjective bialgebra map $\pi : H.\mathrm{level}\,v \to Mt$ which is universal among bialgebra maps from `H.level v` to such Hopf algebras (for each such $M'$ and each $f$ there is a unique $g$ with $g\circ\pi=f$). The conclusion: every point $f$ of $H$ at level $v$ with values in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, whose underlying $O$-algebra map $\mathrm{toAlgHom}\,f$ satisfies $P\bigl(\mathrm{toAlgHom}\,f(a)-\varepsilon_{\mathrm{counit}}(a)\bigr)<1$ for all $a$ (congruence to the identity point modulo the maximal ideal of $P$, the counit image taken through $O$) and $\mathrm{toAlgHom}\,f\circ\varepsilon_v=\mathrm{toAlgHom}\,f$, factors as $\mathrm{toAlgHom}\,f=g\circ\pi$ for some $O$-algebra map $g : Mt \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   This is the finite-level ordinarity statement for the unit-root part of a $p$-divisible group: formal points supported on the idempotent $\varepsilon$ on which $u$ is invertible lie on the largest quotient of multiplicative type, the hypothesis `hFV` expressing that a power of the transpose of the reduction of $u_1$ lies in the two-sided convolution ideal generated by Frobenius and Verschiebung. It is used in the analysis of the Frobenius action on the ordinary part of the Tate module of a modular Jacobian, in the form of the comparison between Frobenius, the Hecke operator $U$ and the diamond operators.
